course: dictionary
lesson: 8310
title: Roar: a loud, deep sound
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To roar is to make a very loud, deep sound, like a lion. A roar is that sound, or the loud noise of a crowd, an engine, the wind or the sea. «The whole class roared» at Max's story, so roar can also mean to laugh very loudly.
explain: Look at the words around roar to find its meaning. «The stags roar and fight» in autumn, and «a laptop roars during a big game», so the clues are animals, machines and loud noise. Roar can be a verb (to roar) or a noun (a roar).
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If «the roar of the crowd» still makes sense with your meaning, you have understood it. When you are not sure, use the clues around the word.
fact: To roar means to make a very loud, deep sound.
fact: A roar is that loud, deep sound, or the loud noise of a crowd, engine, wind or sea.
fact: «Roar with laughter» means to laugh very loudly.
fact: Roar is a verb (roar, roars, roared, roaring) and a noun (a roar, roars).
fact: Lions and tigers roar, and in stories dragons and monsters roar.
exercise: In autumn, «the stags roar and fight» in Richmond Park. What does roar mean here? | To eat slowly | To sleep quietly | To run very fast | *To make a very loud, deep sound
exercise: «The whole class roared» after Max's story. What does roared mean here? | Ran out of the room | Cried quietly | *Laughed very loudly | Fell asleep
exercise: Which phrase means laughing very loudly? | *roar with laughter | roaring engine | the roar of the crowd | roaring fire
test: «A fan blows air over metal fins, which is why a laptop roars during a big game.» What does roars suggest? | A soft, gentle hum | Complete silence and stillness | A bright light | *A loud, deep noise from a hard-working machine
test: Sophie says roar is only for animals. Is she right? | Yes, people never make loud sounds | Yes, but only lions roar | *No, a crowd or an engine can roar too | Yes, roar is only for animals
exam: In which sentence is roar a verb (an action word)? | «The roar of the sea was loud.» | «The roar was deep and long.» | «A roar came from the crowd.» | *«The stags roar and fight in autumn.»
